WEBVTT

00:10.170 --> 00:11.690
<i>A lot happened, but...</i>

00:17.340 --> 00:20.640
<i>I'll draw what I really</i> <i>want to draw once again.</i>

00:25.780 --> 00:29.520
<i>And if there's even just one person</i> <i>looking forward to my books...</i>

00:49.710 --> 00:50.330
Taishi.

00:55.880 --> 00:58.040
I'll... give it...

00:58.550 --> 01:00.140
I'll give it another try!

01:03.020 --> 01:05.080
Welcome back, my brother.

01:06.830 --> 01:10.390
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

01:10.930 --> 01:14.030
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

01:14.030 --> 01:17.590
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

01:17.840 --> 01:20.900
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

01:21.170 --> 01:24.780
<i>It just doesn't get across...</i>
<i>Nani o Shite mo Tsutawarazu</i>

01:24.780 --> 01:28.350
<i>It's just not working right at all.</i>
<i>Umaku Ikanai Bakari de</i>

01:28.350 --> 01:31.710
<i>But even I and everyone else...</i>
<i>Watashi Datte Dare Datte</i>

01:31.920 --> 01:35.410
<i>... have times like that.</i>
<i>Atarimae ni Aru Koto</i>

01:35.520 --> 01:38.890
<i>Those things that don't return to your heart.</i>
<i>Mune no Naka ni Kaeranai</i>

01:39.090 --> 01:42.490
<i>But even those words and feelings...</i>
<i>Omoi mo Kotoba mo Itsuka</i>

01:42.660 --> 01:47.060
<i>... will come back in time someday...</i>
<i>Jikan ga Tateba Modotte Kuru kara</i>

01:47.300 --> 01:50.230
<i>... before you know it.</i>
<i>Shiranai Uchi ni</i>

01:50.500 --> 01:56.440
<i>There's only one thing you can do right now.</i>
<i>Ima Kimiga Dekiru Koto wa Hitotsu</i>

01:56.780 --> 02:03.510
<i>Just accept it and go with it.</i>
<i>Sono Mama Ukeirete Yukou</i>

02:04.150 --> 02:08.190
<i>Just be you and stay true to yourself.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Itsuwarazu ni</i>

02:08.190 --> 02:11.320
<i>Take a little break.</i>
<i>Sukoshi Hitoyasumi Shite</i>

02:11.320 --> 02:15.090
<i>Take your impatience and your hardships...</i>
<i>Aseru Kimochi Kurushii Koto</i>

02:15.090 --> 02:18.360
<i>...and turn them into your strengths.</i>
<i>Kimi no Power ni Kaete</i>

02:18.430 --> 02:22.200
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

02:22.570 --> 02:25.670
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

02:25.670 --> 02:29.270
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

02:29.470 --> 02:32.380
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

02:35.310 --> 02:42.120
BROTHER 2,

02:35.310 --> 02:42.120
ONCE AGAIN

02:43.420 --> 02:46.080
Looks like you're finally back!

02:46.790 --> 02:50.020
Startin' or quittin' doujin work is all up to the person,

02:50.260 --> 02:53.320
but it's always more fun when you've got more friends.

02:53.770 --> 02:54.790
Yuu.

02:54.870 --> 02:56.730
Let's have fun together again!

02:57.440 --> 02:58.300
Yeah!

02:58.300 --> 02:59.460
All right!

02:59.840 --> 03:02.400
We'll have a strategy meeting right after school, please!

03:02.610 --> 03:04.680
On a larger scale than the Normandy Invasion!

03:04.680 --> 03:06.800
Even more intense than the Battle of the Bulge!

03:06.910 --> 03:11.280
Our Brother 2's complete recovery, come back, salmon strategy meeting!

03:11.480 --> 03:13.850
Man, he's totally hyped up.

03:13.950 --> 03:15.650
Well, it's just like him, though.

03:16.860 --> 03:19.450
Comrade Kazuki, constantly swimming upstream against the swift currents!

03:19.990 --> 03:21.630
Splash, splash, splash!

03:20.960 --> 03:22.230
Kazuki...

03:21.830 --> 03:24.320
Show them just how lively you are!

03:29.270 --> 03:30.530
Mizuki!

03:30.940 --> 03:32.530
Hey, Mizuki!

03:36.040 --> 03:38.100
Mi-zu-ki!

03:38.740 --> 03:40.210
What? Oh...

03:40.650 --> 03:42.170
Sheesh, what's wrong?

03:42.250 --> 03:45.080
You've been spaced out ever since we left school.

03:45.420 --> 03:47.720
S-sorry, so what were we talking about?

03:48.120 --> 03:50.180
The Christmas party!

03:50.420 --> 03:52.620
It looks like a lot of college students will be there...

03:52.620 --> 03:54.120
...through Reina's connections.

03:54.260 --> 03:55.690
But is it okay?

03:55.790 --> 03:56.960
You both have entrance exams...

03:56.960 --> 03:59.260
...and all sorts of other things going on after New Year's, right?

03:59.560 --> 04:01.500
At this point, it won't make a difference!

04:01.630 --> 04:05.070
And I'm already done with the forms for the technical institute.

04:06.200 --> 04:07.300
Oh, I see.

04:07.510 --> 04:10.100
In your case, you've got to worry more about graduating.

04:10.610 --> 04:12.170
Don't say that.

04:12.280 --> 04:14.250
Well, I'm sure it'll work out.

04:14.350 --> 04:16.810
Coming from you...

04:20.320 --> 04:23.850
<i>Kazuki's cheered up and I</i> <i>should be happy about it, but...</i>

04:27.890 --> 04:29.220
However!

04:29.490 --> 04:31.800
Our comrade's recovery is great,

04:31.800 --> 04:33.890
but the time left to us is far too short!

04:34.370 --> 04:35.390
That's true.

04:35.470 --> 04:38.770
Well, you'll have to settle for me sellin' it for you.

04:38.840 --> 04:39.770
Selling it for me?

04:39.770 --> 04:43.440
Of course. The winter Comi-Pa's application deadline's been long over.

04:43.580 --> 04:45.480
Oh! That's right...

04:46.580 --> 04:48.140
I guess that's true.

04:49.950 --> 04:53.040
It's okay. Comi-Pa isn't goin' anywhere. There'll be another one.

04:54.990 --> 04:59.420
But I want to make my own book and sell it myself, and...

05:00.430 --> 05:02.120
I understand how you feel, but...

05:04.800 --> 05:07.670
I have been suppressing my laughter for a while now,

05:07.670 --> 05:09.570
as if I am hiding something incredible!

05:09.870 --> 05:12.430
Oh, right, right. So?

05:13.300 --> 05:14.500
I thought it might come to this.

05:15.140 --> 05:18.800
So, I already completed an application to the winter Comi-Pa...

05:20.650 --> 05:22.440
...under the name of Brother 2!

05:24.580 --> 05:28.220
Behold! This envelope with the label indicating acceptance!

05:27.490 --> 05:30.590
Asahi Sakurai

05:27.490 --> 05:30.590
Official Fanclub Headquarters

05:33.520 --> 05:34.790
No!

05:34.790 --> 05:40.530
Th-this is Asahi Sakurai's official fanclub newsletter!

05:41.200 --> 05:44.440
This isn't it! And this isn't it either!

05:42.900 --> 05:44.900
Did you really get accepted?

05:44.970 --> 05:47.910
Believe me! Those who believe shall be saved!

05:47.170 --> 05:48.460
Maybe you forgot it at home?

05:48.910 --> 05:52.040
Impossible! Only yesterday, as part of an early spring cleaning,

05:52.110 --> 05:53.840
I cleaned out my secret library...

05:53.950 --> 05:57.180
...and got rid of unnecessary comics and any duplicates I had!

05:57.280 --> 05:59.650
Everything should be perfectly organized...

06:00.690 --> 06:01.480
Taishi?

06:01.620 --> 06:04.350
Oh, Jesus!

06:06.420 --> 06:08.190
Hurry! We must hurry!

06:08.860 --> 06:10.500
A used comic shop?

06:10.500 --> 06:14.690
Yes! It would be terrible to lose it, so I sandwiched the ticket...

06:14.770 --> 06:19.600
...in the hugely popular comic "Viva
Amazing Icepick Man", which I sold!

06:20.810 --> 06:22.640
W-wait up for me! Hey!

06:23.370 --> 06:26.110
What if the used bookstore sold the comic?!

06:26.480 --> 06:30.210
Worst case scenario, a fake Brother 2 will appear!

06:30.520 --> 06:31.380
Fake?!

06:31.720 --> 06:33.010
Imagined vision, come on!

06:36.350 --> 06:38.520
Th-that would be dangerous!

06:38.720 --> 06:40.950
We must recover it at all costs before that happens!

06:41.990 --> 06:43.690
Hey, you guys!

06:44.230 --> 06:47.030
Let's hurry! Acceleration device, back teeth, click!

06:47.130 --> 06:48.760
I don't get it, but click!

06:48.930 --> 06:51.900
Click, click, click, click!

06:54.770 --> 06:56.240
They're gone...

06:56.410 --> 06:58.880
Oh well. I'll go about it my own way, and...

07:01.610 --> 07:03.010
Yo, Mizuki!

07:03.350 --> 07:04.650
Oh, Yuu.

07:12.520 --> 07:16.090
We broke the sound barrier!

07:17.330 --> 07:18.190
Wh-what was that?!

07:18.960 --> 07:20.430
Mommy!

07:21.070 --> 07:23.500
I see it! It's inside that building!

07:23.500 --> 07:25.160
All right!

07:26.200 --> 07:26.930
BLONDE WAY

07:28.440 --> 07:30.030
Used Book Specialty Store

07:28.440 --> 07:30.030
Comic Store on 4th Floor

07:30.610 --> 07:31.670
Hello, there!

07:32.080 --> 07:34.410
Oh, hi again, Mr. Kuhonbutsu.

07:34.910 --> 07:36.610
We got some nice things in today.

07:36.710 --> 07:39.120
Wh-wh-wh-wh-what about the used books?!

07:39.780 --> 07:42.620
Yes, used books. Please take a look!

07:42.820 --> 07:45.720
A pirated version from back then, of the comic that...

07:45.720 --> 07:48.630
...only has 6 confirmed existing copies in the world!

07:48.860 --> 07:50.800
"The World's Last War!"

07:50.860 --> 07:54.960
No, not that! The used books
I brought in yesterday!

07:55.070 --> 07:57.000
D-did they get sold already?

07:57.200 --> 07:59.570
Let's see... Oh, they're in the storage room.

07:59.900 --> 08:01.570
They haven't been sorted yet.

08:02.240 --> 08:03.730
Saved!

08:14.390 --> 08:16.750
Go ahead, feel free to search through them.

08:18.820 --> 08:20.850
So, from all these...

08:20.990 --> 08:23.660
We have no choice but to look, my brother.

08:26.100 --> 08:28.970
What's up? You don't seem very cheerful.

08:29.300 --> 08:31.290
What? Th-that's not true.

08:33.440 --> 08:35.700
B-by the way, about Kazuki...

08:36.570 --> 08:38.840
He seems to have cheered up.

08:39.180 --> 08:42.440
Yeah, I don't really get it, but he seems to have gotten over it.

08:50.520 --> 08:52.150
<i>I figured it out!</i>

08:55.790 --> 08:59.090
So, Mizuki, you cheer up, too.

08:59.400 --> 09:02.890
Oh, please. I already told you, I'm not...

09:02.970 --> 09:04.270
You're lyin'.

09:04.500 --> 09:06.660
It's good that Kazuki's cheered up,

09:06.900 --> 09:09.430
but he's so absorbed in doujinshi, you're real lonely now, aren't you?

09:09.870 --> 09:11.570
That's not true, I...

09:12.010 --> 09:17.450
I don't really like doujinshi and exhibition and spot sales,

09:17.750 --> 09:19.110
but if Kazuki enjoys them...

09:22.450 --> 09:26.050
"Christmas Sale"

09:26.720 --> 09:27.950
I...

09:30.160 --> 09:32.230
Then you just have to get to like them!

09:32.230 --> 09:34.600
Get to like doujinshi...

09:34.670 --> 09:38.360
...and make books and go to exhibition and spot sales with him.

09:47.750 --> 09:49.610
It's like with Christmas parties.

09:51.020 --> 09:55.290
It's always more fun bein' in the warm room, bein' rowdy with everyone...

09:55.290 --> 09:58.050
...rather than lookin' in the window from the outside.

10:01.930 --> 10:05.360
I love them all. Doujinshi, exhibition and spot sales,

10:06.300 --> 10:07.460
and Kazuki, too.

10:08.570 --> 10:12.070
You don't get many guys these days who're serious almost to a fault...

10:12.070 --> 10:14.560
...and who're nice and earnest.

10:15.110 --> 10:16.570
Oh, but, well...

10:17.110 --> 10:21.510
And I could work with Kazuki, makin' books and bein' a shopgirl.

10:23.010 --> 10:26.010
Well, Mizuki, I'll see ya tomorrow at school!

10:46.700 --> 10:48.670
Have you found it, Taishi?

10:48.810 --> 10:51.070
No! It isn't here, anywhere!

10:51.340 --> 10:54.940
The hugely popular "Viva
Amazing Icepick Man"!

10:55.350 --> 10:58.510
Why?! Why haven't we seen it?!

10:59.050 --> 11:01.610
Not this! Not this! This isn't it, either!

11:01.690 --> 11:02.920
Oh, is this it?!

11:04.460 --> 11:07.190
It's not here! It's not here! It's not here!

11:05.090 --> 11:06.460
Taishi.

11:07.360 --> 11:10.090
Comrade, I am sorry! I am sorry!

11:08.490 --> 11:10.090
That's enough.

11:11.030 --> 11:12.260
Let's give up.

11:12.660 --> 11:14.330
No! Never!

11:14.700 --> 11:16.630
Right when Comrade Kazuki made a complete recovery...

11:16.630 --> 11:20.440
...and Brother 2 was about to truly embark on world conquest!

11:20.710 --> 11:22.870
And all because of one measly envelope...

11:23.170 --> 11:24.680
The Earth may be laid to waste,

11:24.680 --> 11:27.140
but in the name of Brother 2,
I will not permit it!

11:27.550 --> 11:29.840
I am far from giving up!

11:30.180 --> 11:32.310
Just you watch! I shall find it!

11:32.520 --> 11:35.010
Where?! Where is it?!

11:42.590 --> 11:45.090
T-Taishi, are you okay?!

11:48.230 --> 11:50.670
It's okay, already. It can't be helped.

11:53.000 --> 11:54.130
How pitiful.

11:55.540 --> 11:57.270
It is just too pitiful.

11:57.640 --> 11:59.840
I am called the Secret Lord of Exhibition and Spot Sales.

11:59.980 --> 12:01.880
Also known as the Stealth Doujin.

12:02.080 --> 12:05.780
I have also been called the Ultimate Educator.

12:06.080 --> 12:09.050
Hey, hey, I've never heard about any of this.

12:10.120 --> 12:12.090
To think that I ruined the beginning...

12:12.160 --> 12:14.990
...of my brother's comeback event, the winter Comi-Pa.

12:17.630 --> 12:19.190
Say, Taishi?

12:19.330 --> 12:20.330
What?

12:20.330 --> 12:21.670
It's kind of late to be asking this,

12:21.670 --> 12:24.690
but where did you get the idea of working on doujinshi with me?

12:25.300 --> 12:27.510
Knowing you, you probably could've found plenty of other guys...

12:27.510 --> 12:29.630
...who could draw better than me.

12:32.680 --> 12:34.110
World conquest.

12:34.180 --> 12:35.980
I don't mean that old joke.

12:36.080 --> 12:37.670
I'm serious, Comrade.

12:38.750 --> 12:41.620
The projects we work on will be turned into anime shows and movies,

12:41.720 --> 12:43.450
and it will be distributed worldwide.

12:43.590 --> 12:48.490
And numerous people will feel joy, will cry, will laugh, and be moved.

12:49.060 --> 12:52.830
Is this not a grand way to conquer the world through entertainment?

12:53.260 --> 12:55.170
I've already heard all this.

12:55.400 --> 12:58.960
What I want to know is, why did you pick me?

12:59.270 --> 13:00.830
Do you still not understand?

13:01.870 --> 13:04.340
There are plenty of people who can draw well.

13:04.680 --> 13:09.050
But there are not so many whom I can trust from the bottom of my heart.

13:09.710 --> 13:10.920
Taishi?

13:10.920 --> 13:13.680
A passionate will to convey something to others,

13:14.090 --> 13:16.580
in spite of the agony, pain, and suffering.

13:17.520 --> 13:21.080
You can do it. You crawled back up, out of the agony of Hell.

13:22.160 --> 13:23.590
I have faith in you.

13:24.930 --> 13:26.660
Y-you're embarrassing me.

13:27.060 --> 13:28.330
Comrade...

13:28.630 --> 13:30.290
It's a joke!

13:31.000 --> 13:32.200
I knew it.

13:32.370 --> 13:35.360
You've always been telling jokes, ever since kindergarten.

13:35.910 --> 13:37.670
Yes! Ever since kindergarten.

13:39.480 --> 13:42.500
All right! Let's give it one more go!

13:42.650 --> 13:44.170
Our passport to infinity!

13:44.250 --> 13:46.020
So that we may lay our hands...

13:46.020 --> 13:47.890
...on the envelope containing the winter Comi-Pa group ticket!

13:47.890 --> 13:48.940
Yeah!

13:49.020 --> 13:49.950
Um...

13:50.760 --> 13:51.880
I'm sorry!

13:52.090 --> 13:54.060
I asked the manager and he said...

13:54.130 --> 13:56.890
...that he sold all the books Mr.
Kuhonbutsu brought in right away.

14:02.370 --> 14:04.960
I am sorry, my comrade.

14:05.040 --> 14:06.700
Don't let it bother you.

14:06.900 --> 14:08.370
What the heck?

14:08.570 --> 14:11.010
You guys're walkin' with awfully gloomy looks on your faces.

14:11.280 --> 14:12.710
Oh, it's you.

14:13.080 --> 14:14.480
Where have you been?

14:14.480 --> 14:15.580
Here.

14:14.910 --> 14:16.350
Participation Registration Card

14:16.010 --> 14:17.280
Group Name

14:16.010 --> 14:17.280
Group Representative

14:17.720 --> 14:19.050
Why?!

14:19.120 --> 14:20.050
Is that...

14:20.050 --> 14:22.920
It's a genuine group ticket to the winter Comi-Pa.

14:23.450 --> 14:25.450
Wh-wh-where did you get this?!

14:25.660 --> 14:29.720
You silly, they're not unaccommodatin' government officials.

14:29.890 --> 14:31.590
Tell the preparation committee about your situation...

14:31.700 --> 14:33.790
...and they'll respond appropriately.

14:33.860 --> 14:36.530
I see, you got them to reissue the ticket!

14:37.470 --> 14:39.800
Now that I'm thinking calmly, you are exactly right!

14:40.200 --> 14:44.200
Maki was laughin' that of the tens of thousands of participatin' groups,

14:44.310 --> 14:47.040
you guys were the only ones who'd lost the whole thing.

14:49.510 --> 14:51.640
That will have made plenty of impact!

14:51.750 --> 14:53.620
The name of Brother 2 is sure to have resounded...

14:53.620 --> 14:55.110
...throughout the preparation committee!

14:55.750 --> 14:57.380
It is all as I had calculated!

14:57.960 --> 14:58.980
Now, <i>that's</i> a lie.

14:59.420 --> 15:00.520
Yup.

15:00.520 --> 15:02.550
Well, shall we go, my brother?

15:02.730 --> 15:03.790
Go where?

15:03.860 --> 15:06.330
You fool! This is the real thing now!

15:06.830 --> 15:08.890
There is just one week left until the winter Comi-Pa!

15:08.970 --> 15:12.490
It is self-evident that we must make printing arrangements right away!

15:12.800 --> 15:14.800
Oh, right!
We're going to Chisa's place?

15:15.170 --> 15:16.330
Bingo!

15:18.340 --> 15:21.470
That would be impossible, even for you, Sir!

15:21.880 --> 15:23.580
What? I-impossible?

15:24.080 --> 15:27.280
From New Year's cards to
New Year's sales flyers.

15:27.690 --> 15:30.590
We have a mountain of jobs piled up.

15:30.860 --> 15:32.860
We also have a customer who made a big order...

15:32.860 --> 15:34.160
A customer...

15:34.230 --> 15:35.660
...who made a big order?

15:37.230 --> 15:40.690
Hi! Has my new issue been printed?

15:41.570 --> 15:42.430
It's you!

15:43.330 --> 15:44.560
Hot spring panda!

15:44.970 --> 15:47.630
Then, the customer who made the big order is...

15:50.240 --> 15:51.880
Mysterious Labyrinth

15:50.610 --> 15:55.110
Th-these are all the new issue of "Cat or Fish?"!

15:55.250 --> 15:56.450
Why, Eimi?!

15:56.450 --> 15:59.980
I heard that this printer was super-good.

16:00.350 --> 16:02.950
I was a little worried about cabaclacity,

16:03.020 --> 16:04.820
but I tried placing my order here anyway.

16:05.420 --> 16:07.410
What's cabaclacity?

16:07.890 --> 16:09.520
A city with lots of cabaret clubs?

16:10.060 --> 16:12.550
You don't mean "capacity"?

16:14.530 --> 16:16.300
I see, she was trying to say "capacity"!

16:16.370 --> 16:17.390
I see, "capacity".

16:17.500 --> 16:19.340
"Capacity" turned into "cabaclacity".

16:18.240 --> 16:20.300
Shut up! I was worried about that something-city,

16:20.300 --> 16:22.330
but I tried placing my order here anyway!

16:32.380 --> 16:34.180
Oh, they were right!

16:34.250 --> 16:37.550
The solids are completely black and it looks super-good!

16:38.060 --> 16:39.960
Oh, but you ordered so many copies,

16:40.020 --> 16:41.820
we have not finished printing them all yet.

16:42.030 --> 16:43.290
No way!

16:43.490 --> 16:47.630
P-please do not worry. We will make it on time, without fail.

16:47.830 --> 16:49.270
I'm counting on you!

16:49.330 --> 16:53.290
It's an honor to get to print the great, cute Eimi's book.

16:53.500 --> 16:56.530
Maybe the printers will stop workin' at the unusual honor.

16:56.770 --> 16:59.840
Yes, what with the cabaclacity and all.

17:00.110 --> 17:02.980
You there! What're you muttering about?!

17:03.210 --> 17:05.080
Talk about creepy!

17:05.180 --> 17:06.450
Nothin'.

17:07.520 --> 17:10.350
I guess I can't order my printing here then.

17:10.590 --> 17:12.190
I don't believe it!

17:12.190 --> 17:15.130
You still haven't made printing arrangements?!

17:15.190 --> 17:16.720
Stop, Eimi!

17:17.830 --> 17:19.320
Wh-what?

17:20.460 --> 17:22.660
I-I am very sorry.

17:23.330 --> 17:27.500
I am unable to do anything for you.

17:27.970 --> 17:29.870
I-I am very sorry.

17:30.670 --> 17:32.270
It's okay, Chisa.

17:34.780 --> 17:35.980
Thank you.

17:35.980 --> 17:39.940
You know, I read in some book before...

17:40.550 --> 17:44.850
...that old doujinshi were drawn by hand and passed around.

17:45.260 --> 17:48.160
Yes, it is noted in ancient documents...

17:48.430 --> 17:50.450
...that many of the great, legendary comic artists...

17:50.530 --> 17:53.190
...found their start in hand-drawn books that were passed around.

17:53.330 --> 17:57.630
That's super-uncool!
You sell it once and it's all over!

17:57.630 --> 17:59.660
I told you to shut yer mouth!

18:00.470 --> 18:02.810
It's true that you can't sell a hand-drawn book...

18:02.810 --> 18:05.000
...that's meant to be passed around, but now...

18:05.610 --> 18:07.840
We have convenient machines like that one.

18:15.290 --> 18:17.280
Y-you don't mean...

18:17.550 --> 18:20.520
Yeah, that's exactly what I mean.

18:27.900 --> 18:30.990
Being told that so suddenly...

18:31.370 --> 18:34.630
<i>I love them all. Doujinshi,</i> <i>exhibition and spot sales,</i>

18:35.740 --> 18:37.000
<i>and Kazuki, too.</i>

18:37.840 --> 18:42.070
<i>I could work with Kazuki, makin'</i> <i>books and bein'a shopgirl.</i>

18:44.210 --> 18:48.550
If I could help Kazuki, too...

18:55.190 --> 18:58.190
But, what should I do?

18:59.060 --> 19:01.460
I don't even know what I want to do.

19:05.340 --> 19:06.600
Stupid!

19:07.500 --> 19:09.060
You're really going to do this?

19:10.070 --> 19:11.940
I don't know if I can pull it off or not,

19:11.940 --> 19:14.810
Comi-Pa

19:12.440 --> 19:14.580
but I'll do everything I can.

19:15.450 --> 19:16.970
What are you, a moron?!

19:17.110 --> 19:20.950
There's no way you can make a good manuscript in just one week!

19:21.120 --> 19:22.640
No, you never know!

19:23.220 --> 19:26.950
Do you remember the book Kazuki released at Comic Bravo in May?

19:27.090 --> 19:29.930
That thing? I flipped through it.

19:30.130 --> 19:32.400
It was super-rough and his technique was...

19:32.400 --> 19:36.300
But what if I told you he finished drawin' that in just two days?

19:36.530 --> 19:37.160
What?!

19:37.530 --> 19:40.230
And that was his first comic with split panels.

19:40.370 --> 19:42.600
Hah, I can...

19:42.710 --> 19:46.180
You've been keepin' an eye on Kazuki ever since,

19:46.180 --> 19:49.110
'cause you sensed somethin' of his talent, right?

19:49.450 --> 19:51.470
Th-that's not...

19:52.020 --> 19:54.040
Well, we'll just leave it at that.

19:55.250 --> 19:57.790
But you know, just 'cause you spent a long time on it...

19:57.790 --> 20:00.420
...doesn't mean you'll end up with a good manuscript.

20:00.760 --> 20:04.350
And you know that real well, don't you, Eimi?

20:06.100 --> 20:08.160
Well then, shall we begin, my comrade?

20:08.470 --> 20:10.090
First, we begin with storyboards.

20:10.230 --> 20:12.500
No, we must determine the genre before we do that.

20:12.640 --> 20:14.630
No, no, the number of pages comes first.

20:14.710 --> 20:15.870
Thank you, Taishi.

20:17.440 --> 20:19.100
I'm alone in this from here on out.

20:19.340 --> 20:21.640
Wh-why? How come?!

20:21.950 --> 20:23.410
We are Brother 2!

20:23.480 --> 20:24.680
In death and in life,

20:24.680 --> 20:26.720
we are always together except when going to the bathroom!

20:26.720 --> 20:28.780
No, I'll first try it alone.

20:29.390 --> 20:32.080
I'll only ask for help at the very end.

20:32.160 --> 20:33.450
B-but...

20:33.890 --> 20:35.730
You heard what Kazuki said.

20:35.730 --> 20:37.820
But is now not the time to fight together?!

20:38.200 --> 20:40.260
He's already fightin'.

20:40.660 --> 20:41.720
Look.

20:48.210 --> 20:50.210
He has to coax out that "something"...

20:50.210 --> 20:52.840
...deep in his heart that hasn't taken shape yet.

20:53.140 --> 20:54.880
And he has to put that down...

20:54.880 --> 20:58.280
...on the blank sheet of paper with just one black line.

20:58.720 --> 21:01.380
He's already begun to fight on his own.

21:01.450 --> 21:03.750
Super-cheesy! Cheesy!

21:03.920 --> 21:06.190
What a lame-o line!

21:06.390 --> 21:08.380
There's nothin' wrong with bein' lame!

21:09.060 --> 21:12.090
Come on, let's go!
We can't get left behind.

21:12.300 --> 21:14.230
We gotta make flyers and displays!

21:14.430 --> 21:17.300
There's a ton of things to do before the winter Comi-Pa!

21:17.500 --> 21:19.770
Hah! I don't need you to tell me that!

21:20.070 --> 21:22.100
Yeah, yeah, well, let's go!

21:22.440 --> 21:23.370
Yes.

21:23.470 --> 21:26.600
Hey, let me go!
Wh-what are you doing?!

21:28.110 --> 21:30.010
<i>And here, there'll be action...</i>

21:30.080 --> 21:32.240
<i>No, I can't waste pages on this...</i>

21:32.380 --> 21:35.580
<i>I know! I'll leave it to the</i> <i>reader's imagination instead...</i>

21:35.820 --> 21:38.150
<i>I'll try to make the first half...</i>

21:38.220 --> 21:41.450
<i>Hang in there. You're not the</i> <i>only one agonizin' over this.</i>

21:50.330 --> 21:51.570
Stupid.

21:51.570 --> 21:54.000
Stupid, stupid, stupid.

21:54.240 --> 21:56.610
Stupid Mizuki Takase.

22:19.560 --> 22:23.800
<i>The distant sky looked bright...</i>
<i>Touku no Sora ga Akaruku Mieta</i>

22:23.800 --> 22:28.300
<i>...and we began walking.</i>
<i>Soshite Bokura wa Arukihajimeta</i>

22:28.410 --> 22:32.810
<i>Getting our feet caught in the mud.</i>
<i>Nukarumi ni Ashi o Torarenagara</i>

22:32.980 --> 22:36.880
<i>Heading for a shapeless city.</i>
<i>Katachi no Nai Machi o Mezashite</i>

22:36.880 --> 22:40.980
<i>The pocket in my heart was full...</i>
<i>Kokoro no Naka no Pocket ni wa</i>

22:40.980 --> 22:45.250
<i>...of the grownup things we'd just learned.</i>
<i>Oboetate no Otona ga Ippai</i>

22:45.460 --> 22:49.860
<i>Having taken off our uniforms...</i>
<i>Seifuku o Nuida Bokura ni wa</i>

22:49.990 --> 22:54.030
<i>... the wind was just a little too cold.</i>
<i>Kaze wa Sukoshi Tsumetasugita</i>

22:54.030 --> 22:57.570
<i>Who in the world am I?</i>
<i>Ittai Boku wa Dare Darou</i>

22:57.570 --> 23:02.510
<i>I think about that every so often.</i>
<i>Tokidoki Sonna Koto o Omou</i>

23:02.640 --> 23:06.140
<i>In the world outside the school building...</i>
<i>Kousha no Soto no Sekai de wa</i>

23:06.140 --> 23:11.580
<i>...it's like everyone is a</i> <i>pawn in a game of chess.</i>
<i>Daremo ga Marude Chess no Koma sa</i>

23:12.650 --> 23:17.090
<i>I'm here for you.</i>
<i>Kimi no Tame ni Boku ga Ite</i>

23:17.090 --> 23:21.120
<i>And you for me.</i>
<i>Boku no Tame ni Kimiga</i>

23:21.120 --> 23:25.660
<i>When you think about that...</i>
<i>Sou Omoeba Daremo ga</i>

23:25.660 --> 23:34.630
<i>... everyone is needed by someone.</i>
<i>Dareka no Tame ni Hitsuyou sa</i>

23:55.260 --> 24:19.420
PREVIEW

23:57.960 --> 23:59.600
The deadline is approaching!

23:59.600 --> 24:01.870
Will Kazuki be able to finish his manuscript?!

24:02.170 --> 24:04.630
And will Mizuki ignore Kazuki...

24:04.630 --> 24:08.370
...and go to the gathering, which is the Christmas party?!

24:08.370 --> 24:09.670
And the conclusion to that...

24:09.670 --> 24:11.040
The conclusion is?

24:11.640 --> 24:13.280
...will have to wait until the next episode!

24:13.280 --> 24:14.340
What?!

24:14.340 --> 24:17.150
And so, with that predictable and forced lure...

24:17.150 --> 24:18.380
Next time...

24:18.380 --> 24:20.080
"Our Party!"

24:20.080 --> 24:22.690
Our legend is about to begin now.

24:20.080 --> 24:25.090
NEXT TIME

24:20.080 --> 24:25.090
OUR PARTY!
